---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Call for Contributors">
  <div class="cta-hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">🚀 Call for Contributors</div>
    <h1>A modular, AI-optional TTRPG ecosystem — built for hackers, storytellers, and curious devs.</h1>
    <p class="tagline">Fate's Edge is an open, extensible tabletop RPG platform — rules engine, AI GM, multi-client transport layer, voice stack, and VTT surfaces — all designed around one principle.</p>
    <p class="principle">Every layer should be replaceable, hackable, and fun to build on.</p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-gold" href="/contribute">Ways to Contribute</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/architecture">Read the Architecture</a>
      <a class="btn btn-outline" href="https://github.com/Chronophage-net/fate-edge-dev/discussions">Join the Discussion</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="section lead" style="margin-top:-1rem;">If you love clean architecture, real-time systems, game design, or AI-assisted storytelling, this project is a playground. We're looking for contributors who want to help shape the future of open TTRPG tech.</p>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>🌐 What makes Fate's Edge special</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="feature-card"><span class="icon">🎲</span><h3>One elegant resolution mechanic</h3><p>Easy to extend, easy to automate.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><span class="icon">⚙️</span><h3>Deterministic rules engine</h3><p>No hidden GM logic, no opaque heuristics.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><span class="icon">🔌</span><h3>Interoperable transport layer</h3><p>Web, desktop, terminal, Discord, Roll20, Foundry, Python.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><span class="icon">🏷️</span><h3>Tag-based GM protocol</h3><p>Safe, test-covered, and easy to extend.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><span class="icon">🤖</span><h3>Modular AI GM</h3><p>Driver-agnostic, state-machine-driven, and fully optional.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><span class="icon">🎙️</span><h3>Voice pipeline</h3><p>TTS, ambience, and cloning — all toggleable.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><span class="icon">🧱</span><h3>Layered architecture</h3><p>Every subsystem can be swapped without breaking the rest.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="lead">If you enjoy building systems that feel alive, Fate's Edge is your kind of project.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>🛠️ Ways you can contribute</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Extend the Tag DSL</h3><p>Add new GM directives, narrative tools, or mechanical hooks.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Build new client surfaces</h3><p>Mobile app, Slack bot, custom VTT — anything that speaks the room protocol.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Add new LLM drivers</h3><p>Anthropic, Groq, Gemini, local models.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Improve the transport layer</h3><p>Event parity, reliability, scaling.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Author adventure modules</h3><p>JSON-based, rules-native, AI-optional.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Expand the voice stack</h3><p>New TTS engines, ambience systems, or adapters.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Enhance the web client</h3><p>VTT tools, offline mode, UI polish.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Contribute to the terminal client</h3><p>ANSI UI, WS protocol, dice UX.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Write docs and examples</h3><p>Tutorials, diagrams, onboarding guides.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="lead">Whether you're a seasoned engineer or a curious hobbyist, there's a place for you here. See the full <a href="/contribute">Ways to Contribute guide</a> for guided links into each area.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>🔍 What contributors can expect</h2>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Real boundaries</h3><p>A clear architecture, not a tangle.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>A responsive maintainer</h3><p>Nick reads every issue and PR.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>A safety net</h3><p>A test-covered core that makes contributions safe.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>A welcoming community</h3><p>Builders and storytellers, side by side.</p></div>
      <div class="feature-card"><h3>Fun to hack on</h3><p>Not just functional — enjoyable.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="lead">This isn't a monolithic engine. It's a system of systems, each small enough to understand and big enough to matter.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>🌱 How to get started</strong>
      <ol style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0 1.2rem; color: var(--text);">
        <li>Clone the repos below.</li>
        <li>Read the <a href="/architecture">architecture overview</a>.</li>
        <li>Pick a subsystem that sparks your interest.</li>
        <li>Open an issue or draft a PR — even tiny contributions are welcome.</li>
        <li><a href="https://github.com/Chronophage-net/fate-edge-dev/discussions">Join the conversation</a>, share ideas, and help shape the future of the project.</li>
        <li>See the full <a href="/workflow">dev workflow</a> — how Discuss → Issue → PR maps onto these repos, and where the <a href="https://github.com/Chronophage-net/fate-edge-dev/wiki">wiki</a> fits in.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <ul class="repo-list">
      <li><a href="https://github.com/Chronophage-net/fates-edge-ai-gm-bot">github.com/Chronophage-net/fates-edge-ai-gm-bot</a> — rules engine, AI GM, transport layer</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/Chronophage-net/fates-edge-apps">github.com/Chronophage-net/fates-edge-apps</a> — web client, terminal client, tools</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="text-align:center; padding-block: 1rem 3rem;">
    <h2 style="border:none;">💬 Final note</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="margin: 0 auto;">Fate's Edge is a love letter to the TTRPG hobby — built to be shared, remixed, extended, and enjoyed. If you want to help build the next generation of open tabletop tools, we'd be thrilled to have you.</p>
    <div class="btn-row" style="justify-content:center; margin-top: 1rem;">
      <a class="btn btn-gold" href="https://github.com/Chronophage-net/fate-edge-dev/discussions">Say hello in Discussions</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
